  "description": "Your Exposure Campagnolo\n\nTHE LATEST EVOLUTION OF OUR UNIQUE MASON EXPOSURE, WITH CONFIGURABLE SRAM BUILD OPTIONS\n\nOur Italian-made Dedacciai steel bikepacking and adventure bicycle. Designed with larger clearances and more relaxed geometry, the Exposure is highly adaptable with multiple load and accessory-carrying configurations.\n\nMasterpiece is a pretty big word to throw into a bike review, but I’m as comfortable and excited about using it here\n\n– Bike Perfect 2023\n\nThis lovingly crafted bicycle is developed for fast, long-distance, extended adventure touring over very variable and unpredictable terrain. It's designed with capacity for 650b x 58mm [2.35”] and 700c x 56mm tyres. Campagniolo groupsets provide the perfect complement to this handcrafted Italian frame.\n\nThe Exposure's custom-shaped, progressively butted, phosphate-coated Dedacciai Zero Uno tubeset is engineered by Dedacciai for long range riding, with class-leading toughness and weight, combined with engaging pedalling feel, ride quality and efficiency. The Reynolds 631 44mm head tube is CNC-machined by Bear exclusively for the Exposure.\n\nA recent update brings MASON-designed CNC-machined dropouts to the Exposure, compatible with the Universal Derailleur Hanger standard.\n\nThis frame is paired with a MASON full-carbon fork – the RangeFinder AS ['AS' for AdventureSport] - which is tuned for all surface riding conditions. The Rangefinder AS features a full set of moulded-in eyelets, and is designed to be fitted with a front rack or rando-style bag support, along with accessory cages and internally routed dynamo light.\n\nAvailable with Super Record 13, EKAR or a choice of other Campagnolo groupsets\n\nAvailable with a choice of HUNT, DT Swiss and Campagnolo wheelsets in 700c or 650b. Other options available on request\n\nFrame clearance with capacity for 650b x 58mm [2.25”] and 700c x 55mm tyres. [700c x 45mm approx. including mudguards]\n\nAvailable with a choice of the best 650B or 700C tyres from Panaracer, WTB, Rene Herse and Schwalbe\n\nChoice of finishing kit from Deda, Ritchey and many other brands\n\nCarbon MASON Penta microadjust seatpost and MASON Macro seatclamp\n\nOptional MASON Luminance Upgrade: dynamo and lighting set-up for all-season adventures\n\nCOLOURS AVAILABLE: FilterYellow. OpticGreen. AccursedOchre [Please Request]. DiffuserBlack Metallic.\n\nDiscreet internal dynamo-light top tube routing with stainless steel port reinforcement\n\n100% Italian TIG-welded/silver-brazed frame manufacturing, wet-painting and finishing\n\nUK-made 44mm head tube machined by Bear from Reynolds 631 steel for a semi-integrated headset\n\nBottle/accessory cage boss placements as standard: 4 down tube (top side); 3 down tube (underneath); 3 seat tube; 2 top tube, 2 seat stays (both sides)\n\nDiscreet internal dynamo-light top tube routing with stainless steel port reinforcement\n\nClearance for 48/31T double chainset | 40T single chainring\n\nChain pip neatly holds the chain on the chainring whilst the wheel is removed for travelling",
